diff --git a/CHANGES.md b/CHANGES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c46ed87
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CHANGES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Changes relative to the upstream code
+
+Upstream: https://github.com/DavisWeaver/evo_dm, commit `d975114` (GPL-3.0). This fork keeps the
+upstream licence file and is released under GPL-3.0. Everything not listed here is unchanged upstream code.
+
+## Modified upstream files
+- `evodm/evol_game.py`: new `obs_delay` argument and three `train_input` modes (`delayed_state`,
+  `delayed_history`, `delayed_decoy`); histories of states and drugs; `build_obs()`; `OBS_STALE`
+  (real staleness of the reading, separate from `OBS_DELAY`, the window length the network was built for);
+  new input shapes; replay tuples built from the delayed observation in `define_sensor`.
+- `evodm/learner.py`: `OBS_DELAY` hyperparameter passed to the environment; the Dense network
+  is used for the new modes; `get_qs` reads the current observation for the new modes.
+- `evodm/exp.py`: `obs_delay` argument of `evol_deepmind`.
+
+## New files (mine)
+- `evodm/evaluate.py`: greedy evaluation of a trained agent (no exploration, no learning), with
+  optional mismatched staleness, and evaluation of the random and exact-optimum reference policies.
+- `run_experiment.py`: runs one experiment from a configuration file and writes the raw results and a run record.
+- `run_baseline.py`: earlier command-line runner, used for the pilot runs (results `baseline_*`, `state_*`,
+  `history_*`, `decoy_*` with `_ep200_` or `_ep500_` in their names); kept for traceability.
+- `scripts/make_configs.py`, `scripts/run_all.sh`: build and run every configuration.
+- `configs/main/`: one configuration file per experiment in the paper.
+- `evodm/test/test_delay_obs.py`, `evodm/test/test_mismatch_eval.py`: tests for the new code.
+- `REPRODUCTION.md`, `DESIGN_FREEZE.md`, `EXPERIMENTS.md`, `CHANGES.md`: documentation.
+
+## Not changed
+The evolutionary simulator, the landscapes, the Q-learning update, the replay and exploration logic, the
+exact optimum (backward induction) and the random policy.
diff --git a/DESIGN_FREEZE.md b/DESIGN_FREEZE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..07a53e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DESIGN_FREEZE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Design freeze (written before any main run)
+
+DRAFT: Sai to read, edit and commit this file before starting `scripts/run_all.sh`. After the first main run,
+only typos may change; anything else is recorded as a deviation at the end of this file.
+
+## Question
+When the genotype reading is delayed, does telling the agent which drugs were given since that reading
+restore performance, and is the benefit specific to the real drug record?
+
+## Conditions (all use the same untuned hyperparameters, 500 episodes, `train_freq=1`)
+- `state`: sees only the stale genotype distribution (control for the contribution).
+- `history`: stale genotype plus the drugs given since (contribution).
+- `decoy`: stale genotype plus random drugs, same input size as `history` (control for input size).
+- `state` at delay 0: the no-delay reference with the same Dense network.
+- `repo` at delay 0: the repository's own Conv1D agent at the same budget (matched-budget reproduction).
+- Delays 1, 2 and 3. Reference policies: random drugs and the exact optimum, evaluated on the same protocol.
+
+## Seeds
+Seeds 10 to 14 for every condition; seeds 15 to 17 are added for the delay-2 conditions only.
+Seeds 0 to 4 were used in pilots and are not reused.
+
+## Primary outcome
+Mean fitness over 50 greedy evaluation episodes at the training delay (no exploration, no learning), per
+run; lower is better. Secondary: share of the optimum's benefit retained, (naive minus RL) / (naive minus DP).
+
+## Hypotheses and decision rules (95% t-intervals on paired differences, pairing by seed)
+- H1: at delays 2 and 3, history minus state is at most -0.15 and the interval excludes zero.
+  (Delay 2 uses seeds 10 to 17, t = 2.365 with 7 degrees of freedom; delay 3 uses seeds 10 to 14, t = 2.776 with 4.)
+- H2: at delays 2 and 3, history minus decoy is at most -0.10 and the interval excludes zero.
+- H3: for a history agent trained at delay 2 and evaluated at staleness 1 and 3, history minus state (same
+  training delay, same test staleness) is at most -0.10 with the interval excluding zero.
+- Delay 1 is exploratory: reported with intervals, with no threshold.
+A hypothesis that misses its threshold is reported as not supported. No threshold is changed after the runs.
+
+## Secondary analyses (stated in advance)
+- Learning curves for every condition (training fitness per episode block).
+- What each agent learns: drug-use frequencies, action entropy, and agreement with the exact optimal policy,
+  computed from the logged actions.
+- Dense versus Conv1D at delay 0, reported as a limitation.
+
+## Alternative explanations to test
+Input size (decoy), too little training (learning curves), fewer stored transitions in the repository's own
+delay option, seed variation (intervals and per-seed points).
+
+## Compute
+About 64 runs. One 500-episode run plus evaluation takes about 6 to 7 minutes in a batch of four on the
+M1 MacBook Air (8 GB), so about 7 hours in total. To be measured and recorded.
+
+## Deviations
+(none yet)
diff --git a/EXPERIMENTS.md b/EXPERIMENTS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..29e8804
--- /dev/null
+++ b/EXPERIMENTS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Running the experiments
+
+All commands run from the repository root in the conda environment `antibio` (Python 3.9, TensorFlow 2.11;
+exact versions in `environment.yml` and `requirements-frozen.txt`).
+
+1. Install: `python -m pip install -e .`
+2. Tests: `python -m pytest evodm/test -q --deselect evodm/test/test_evol_game.py::test_init_dense`
+3. Write the configuration files (already committed): `python scripts/make_configs.py`
+4. Run one experiment: `python run_experiment.py configs/main/main_history_d2_s10.json`
+5. Run all of them, 4 in parallel (finished runs are skipped): `caffeinate -i scripts/run_all.sh`
+
+Each run writes to `results/raw/`: `<id>.csv` (per-episode fitness during training), `<id>_eval.csv`
+(greedy evaluation on fresh episodes) and `<id>_record.json` (configuration, git commit, software versions,
+hardware, compute time). Logs go to `logs/`.
+
+Modes: `repo` = the repository's own agent (Conv1D, true current state); `state` = stale genotype only;
+`history` = stale genotype plus the drugs given since; `decoy` = stale genotype plus random drugs
+(same input size as `history`). Delay and seed are in the configuration file.
